# Multi-Hat Isolation Policy (Mandatory)

`event_loop.execution_mode` + hat count follow a **fixed threshold** — no exemptions:

- **3-hat limit (coordinator mode)**: `hats` count ≤ 3 → preset may use `execution_mode: coordinator` (default) or `execution_mode: isolated`.
- **4+ hats must be explicitly isolated**: `hats` count ≥ 4 → `event_loop.execution_mode: isolated` is **mandatory**. Missing, wrong value, or commented out → preset startup rejected by `preset_lint::check_multi_hat_isolation`.
- **Error message fixed**: `preset declares N hats which exceeds the coordinator limit of 3; set \`event_loop.execution_mode: isolated\` to run this preset` — callers match this literal to localize root cause.
- **No exemptions**: env vars (`RALPH_ALLOW_COORDINATOR_OVERRIDE`), test switches, preset-name exemptions all **unavailable**. All builtin 4+ hat presets already migrated to isolated (U6 commit `2a29e24`).

## Isolated 终态 Authority (U3)

In `execution_mode: isolated`, **all agent terminal states** (completion, review verdict, report completion, plan blocked) must be explicitly listed in the hat's `publishes`:

- Topics NOT in `publishes` (e.g. bare `LOOP_COMPLETE`, undeclared `report.done`, undeclared `review.complete`) are directly rejected by `EventOriginGuard`
- Rejection emits `event.isolation.boundary_violation` diagnostic to `recovery.jsonl` + injects `task.resume` so the agent sees the failure reason
- Same rule applies to `default_publishes` fallback: fallback topics must also be in `publishes`
- **Only exception**: `hat=ralph` runtime builtin hat — `HatRegistry::from_runtime_config()` injects `LOOP_COMPLETE` / `work.start` / `loop.cancel`. Single exemption.

## Isolated Fair Scheduling (U4)

`EventBus` uses **round-robin cursor** (NOT lexicographic first) to pick the next hat in isolated mode:

- After a single event triggers multiple pending hats, cursor advances past the current hat and resumes from that position next time
- Prevents starvation from "always pick alphabetically-first hat"
- Lexicographic first behavior **removed** — don't document old behavior in docs/tests/prompts

## 上限 + 调度 + 终态 Interaction

- 3-hat coordinator preset: not bound by isolated terminal authority / fair scheduling (uses single-prompt multi-hat path)
- 4+ hat isolated preset **must simultaneously satisfy**: `execution_mode=isolated` + every terminal topic in `publishes` + no lexicographic-order dependency
- Any preset validation failure → blocked by `ralph preset check` / `ralph preflight` / `ralph run` startup hard gate — runtime never enters half-started state

## Historical Anti-Pattern: serial preset agent-output governance

> **Status (2026-07-08)**: With plan 2026-07-07-006 the legacy serial CE
> preset is removed from the public surface. The hooks below were
> opt-in flags the dropped preset enabled to defend against its own
> multi-consumer / fallback-success anti-patterns. After the
> single-chain refactor, pipeline covers the same semantics through
> `topic_deny_rules` + isolated terminal authority + `task.resume`
> recovery; the opt-in flags below are no longer exported by any
> builtin preset. Kept here so reviewers can recognise the historical
> anti-patterns if they resurface in a custom preset.
>
> | Hook | Purpose (historical) |
> |------|----------------------|
> | `event_loop.ephemeral_isolation` | Reclaim stray scratchpad files left in source tree by hat prompts |
> | `event_loop.enforce_current_unit` | Reject `task ensure` that re-uses `(loop_id, plan_name, step)` for a different unit |
> | `R1` wave-context injection | Inject last-N-events block when `review-synthesizer` wakes |
> | `R5` policy-rejection routing | Route `task.resume` back to source hat instead of lex-first |
> | `R6` incomplete-wave gate | Auto-emit `plan.blocked` when `received < expected` past `0.8 * aggregate_timeout_secs` |
>
> **Reviewer signal**: any new preset that re-enables one of these
> without documenting why single-chain semantics cannot express the
> need is a regression risk. Prefer pipeline-style (`execution_mode:
> isolated` + `topic_deny_rules`) and let executor own subagent work
> internally.

## Preset System Single-Source-Of-Truth

`presets/manifest.yml` is the **single source of truth** for builtin presets (`crates/ralph-cli/build.rs` + `crates/ralph-cli/src/presets.rs` both read from here, panic on inconsistency). Adding/renaming/deleting a builtin preset MUST sync **4 places**:

1. `presets/en/<name>.yml` (actual YAML)
2. `presets/manifest.yml`'s `embedded:` list
3. `crates/ralph-cli/src/presets.rs` PRESETS array (`EmbeddedPreset { name, description, content, public }`)
4. `presets/index.json` (if user-visible)
5. Sync update CLAUDE.md "Presets & Hats System" builtin list + `scripts/ralph-zsh-plugin.zsh` zsh completion

**Builtin presets** (2026-07-08 single-chain refactor + 2026-07-16-001 test-stabilizer + 2026-07-23-001 supervisor closure + 2026-07-23-005 supervisor dependency-aware pipeline): `autoresearch`, `ce-executor-pipeline` (14-hat linear one-shot **Ralph primary path**: plan-reviewer → executor → `test-stabilizer` (one post-executor stabilization gate) → 6 serial dimension hats → review-synthesizer → fix-planner → fixer (full-suite verification) → alignment → reporter), `ce-executor-pipeline-loop` (16-hat; work.done passes through `test-stabilizer` once, while fix.done routes directly to review-reentry for the next review round), `ce-executor-supervisor` (12 functional hats post-2026-07-23-005 plan U8 — `progress-steward`, `shipper`, fallback `fixer` deleted; topology is `coordinator` → `task-planner` (dependency auditor + execution-plan artifact) → `exec-wave-dispatcher` (dependency-aware iterative ready waves) → `worker` (per-slot TDD) → `exec-integrator` / `exec-failure-handler` → `review-coordinator` (7-dim shared-readonly wave: testing + 6 review dims + merge-conflict) → `review-batch-worker` (×7) → `review-synthesizer` → `fix-task-planner` → `fix-worker` → `fix-integrator` → `alignment` (read-only) → `reporter` (single owner of plan.complete / plan.blocked and the only LOOP_COMPLETE emitter); rusqlite-backed supervisor wave orchestration with default `supervisor-db` feature; per-slot worktrees, fan-in merge, parallel review/fix; **enabled by** `event_loop.supervisor.enabled: true` — no extra build flag needed since the `supervisor-db` feature ships in the default feature set), `ce-executor-lite` (template), `debug`, `merge-batch` (Git-first multi-worktree batch merge), `merge-loop` (the bare legacy CE preset and all its serial/isolated/wave variants all deleted: all plan-driven execution uses `ce-executor-pipeline`; template-only use `ce-executor-lite`).

**Artifact-first terminal reporting:** 终态 reporter 不得把 main event history 当作报告业务输入。`ralph events --events-source main` 在 reporter activation 中仅用于诊断、审计和 wave 写盘确认；报告状态必须来自当前 trigger payload，复杂聚合由上游先写入版本化、可校验的 repo-relative artifact，再把路径随 trigger 传递。reporter 必须按该 artifact 生成报告，不能通过扫描历史重建执行、评审、修复或对齐事实。

State projection design walkthrough v3: `docs/solutions/state-management/proposal-state-projection-design-walkthrough-v3.md`. State-management primitives (current_step derivation, dedup hit counter, envelope `triggered` check, anchor marker) are covered by the U1–U9 units of plan 2026-07-05-005 — see `.cursor/rules/state-management.mdc` for the file-anchor map.

## Wave Config Fields

```yaml
hats:
  reviewer:
    triggers: ["review.file"]
    publishes: ["review.done"]
    concurrency: 4              # Max parallel workers (default: 1)
    instructions: "..."

  synthesizer:
    triggers: ["review.done"]
    publishes: ["review.complete"]
    aggregate:                   # Buffer results until all arrive
      mode: wait_for_all
      timeout: 300               # Seconds to wait
```

- `concurrency > 1` enables wave execution for a hat
- `aggregate` makes a hat wait for all wave results before activating
- A hat cannot have both `concurrency > 1` and `aggregate`
- `missing_event_grace_secs` (optional): per-hat missing-event gate grace period (2026-06-17-004 U2, protects long-running hats like `dimension-reviewer` from first-round silence). Resolve chain: `per-hat → preset → min(idle_timeout*0.3, 540)`. Set `0` to explicitly disable grace. Code: `crates/ralph-core/src/config/hat.rs::resolve_missing_event_grace_secs`, `crates/ralph-cli/src/loop_runner/hard_gate.rs::should_gate_missing_events`
